          }
        }
      },
      "power": {
        "value": 1.8518518518518519,
        "unit": "W",
        "basis": { "sustained": { "average": "mean", "tau": { "value": 0.0102, "unit": "s", "source": { "closed_form": { "note": "The sheet gives no pulse rating to fit, so this is the 10.2 ms default, five periods of a 490 Hz PWM." } } } } },
        "source": {
          "closed_form": {
            "note": "(125 C - 25 C) / 54 C/W. 125 C is the LM7805 operating junction maximum, and the absolute-maximum note gives the TO-220 (NDE) junction-to-ambient thermal resistance as 54 C/W. Shutdown is above 150 C. The thermal table's 23.9 C/W is a board figure. This rating is the bare part, so a breadboard warns before the 1.5 A current rating does."
          }
        }
      },
      "input_voltage": { "value": 35, "unit": "V", "source": { "datasheet": { "doc": "TI SNOSBT0L, LM340, LM340A, LM7805, LM7812, LM7815, February 2000, revised September 2016", "at": "Section 6.1 Absolute Maximum Ratings, DC input voltage, 35 V", "basis": "absolute_max" } } },
    },
    "pins": { "in": "IN", "out": "OUT", "gnd": "GND" }
  },
  "not_simulated": [
    {
      "what": "dropout shape",
      "why": "The sheet states one dropout: 2 V typical at 1 A and 25 C. The model holds that drop. Figure 11 shows a smaller drop at a lighter current, and at a light load a real part can still be in regulation where this model has already dropped out."
    },
    {
      "what": "ground current shape",
      "why": "Ground current stays at about 4.6 mA, the Figure 9 read at 25 C. The table's maximum is 8 mA. The 0.5 mA typical change from 5 mA to 1 A is over temperature, and the model has no load term."
    },
    {
      "what": "foldback current limit",
      "why": "The limit is flat at the 2.4 A peak typical. A short sits about 1 percent above that. The short-circuit typical is 2.1 A, and Figure 10 shows the peak falling as the input-to-output gap grows."
    },
    {
      "what": "thermal shutdown and the input diode",
      "why": "The sheet shuts the regulator down above 150 C. The model has no shutdown, and the power rating warns instead. Reverse current from the output to the input is blocked."
    },
    {
      "what": "ripple rejection, noise, and the 1 kHz output impedance",
      "why": "Ripple rejection is 80 dB typical and output noise is 40 µV typical. Neither is modelled. The 8 mΩ row is the output impedance at 1 kHz. output_resistance is the DC load-regulation slope, about 6.7 mΩ."
    }
  ]
}
